contract-receipt: The origin-tile recurrence of 0 -> 1, 1 -> 0 1^k 2, 2 -> 001 is evaluated by exact sign queries at beta. For k = 2..6 every interior lattice tile with coordinates of absolute value at most 5 reaches the three-phase cycle (1;1,0,0) -> (1;-1,1,0) -> (1;0,0,1) or the vertex cycle (0;0,0,0) -> (1;0,0,0) and no other cycle. At k = 1 the three-phase cycle does not exist and the only interior cycle the same box reaches is one eight-cycle. At k = 2 in box 8, the exact longest transient is 18. The tile (1;8,2,-8) first reaches the cycle at (1;-1,1,0) on step 18, and the census refuses step cap 17. For k = 2..6 no origin child in box 5 has a larger window range max - min of {0, 3 v1 - 1, 3 (v1 + v2) - 2}. At k = 1 the child (1;1,-1,1) of (0;-2,1,0) raises it from 2 to 4. A parameter below one and a tile not covering the origin raise. The cycle census concerns only the named boxes.
